Little pun.

49
00:01:33.110 --> 00:01:34.730
All right, hey, I love this next story.

50
00:01:34.730 --> 00:01:36.310
It comes all the way from Poland.

51
00:01:36.310 --> 00:01:38.430
Apartment Therapy reports a group there

52
00:01:38.430 --> 00:01:40.690
is trying to fight loneliness

53
00:01:40.690 --> 00:01:43.352
with something called Happy to Chat benches.

54
00:01:43.352 --> 00:01:44.185
Oh.

55
00:01:44.185 --> 00:01:45.170
These benches they're special.

56
00:01:45.170 --> 00:01:47.140
And they've been installed in public parks.

57
00:01:47.140 --> 00:01:50.020
They encourage a connection between strangers.

58
00:01:50.020 --> 00:01:52.230
Instructions are printed right there on the bench.

59
00:01:52.230 --> 00:01:53.350 line:15%
It says, "Sit here,

60
00:01:53.350 --> 00:01:56.450 line:15%
if you don't mind stopping to say hello."

61
00:01:56.450 --> 00:01:59.160 line:15%
Now, it's like your Forest Gump fantasy.

62
00:01:59.160 --> 00:02:01.070
If you are feeling a little lonely

63
00:02:01.070 --> 00:02:01.990
and you wanna sit down

64
00:02:01.990 --> 00:02:03.830
and just meet a stranger,

65
00:02:03.830 --> 00:02:04.663
find somebody else,

66
00:02:04.663 --> 00:02:07.330
get a glimpse, a window into somebody else's life.

67
00:02:07.330 --> 00:02:08.570
This is the bench for you.

68
00:02:08.570 --> 00:02:11.610
And I love things that are designated areas to meet people.

69
00:02:11.610 --> 00:02:13.630
It's why I love singles nights at bars

70
00:02:13.630 --> 00:02:15.160
because it's like, "Go here.
Yep.

71
00:02:15.160 --> 00:02:16.640
Everyone's in the mood to meet somebody."

72
00:02:16.640 --> 00:02:17.760
Well, on this bench,

73
00:02:17.760 --> 00:02:19.530
You can meet your next best friend.

74
00:02:19.530 --> 00:02:22.513
I love this, I really do.

75
00:02:23.659 --> 00:02:27.040
I lived on my own in my first apartment when I was 14

76
00:02:27.040 --> 00:02:28.990
and I wasn't able to drive.

77
00:02:28.990 --> 00:02:31.950
And I lived in Los Angeles, which is not a walking city.

78
00:02:31.950 --> 00:02:34.060
And sometimes I would take the bus

79
00:02:34.060 --> 00:02:37.960
and I had just read this book called Desiderata.

80
00:02:37.960 --> 00:02:40.317
And it had this caption in it that said,

81
00:02:40.317 --> 00:02:44.650
"Listen to people, for they have their stories too."

82
00:02:44.650 --> 00:02:46.750 line:15%
And when I read that,

83
00:02:46.750 --> 00:02:47.960 line:15%
I fell so in love with it.

84
00:02:47.960 --> 00:02:50.870 line:15%
It changed my life and I was riding the bus a lot.

85
00:02:50.870 --> 00:02:53.910 line:15%
So a bus bench was a great place for me

86
00:02:53.910 --> 00:02:57.160 line:15%
to hear people's stories and strike up conversation.

87
00:02:57.160 --> 00:02:57.993 line:15%
That's so cute.

88
00:02:57.993 --> 00:02:59.260
And you know what, I feel like you do that

89
00:02:59.260 --> 00:03:01.760
on this show every day, is we meet people.

90
00:03:01.760 --> 00:03:02.820
We find their stories

91
00:03:02.820 --> 00:03:04.870
and we're inspired by them every single day.

92
00:03:04.870 --> 00:03:06.430
And I would encourage anybody out there

93
00:03:06.430 --> 00:03:07.940
